    "narrative": "For LawDog\u2019s July 1st slate, our offensive ceiling is anchored by **Taylor Ward** (71.46) and **Jonathan Aranda** (70.46). **Taylor Ward** benefits from a high-run-environment park factor and a favorable matchup against a struggling Schultz, while **Jonathan Aranda** exploits a strong SP skill matchup against Lugo, pushing him well into our \u201cStrong\u201d tier. We are also heavily leaning into the stolen base potential provided by **Daulton Varsho** (67.28) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.64); both are facing pitchers with slow deliveries, which historically elevates their efficiency scores given our strategy to emphasize speed as a scarcity asset.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the marginal slot occupied by **Geraldo Perdomo** (56.86) over the bench option **Lawrence Butler** (41.52). While **Lawrence Butler** carries a solid park factor, the optimizer docked his score significantly due to a difficult platoon disadvantage and a tough outing against the arm of Dreyer (2.96 xERA). Conversely, **Geraldo Perdomo** remains in the lineup due to his high-leverage spot in the order, though we are monitoring the risk associated with his platoon splits. \n\nWe must remain cautious with **Bryson Stott** (49.79), whose efficiency is suppressed by an elite matchup against Skenes. Despite the talent, Skenes represents a significant hurdle that threatens our batting average and RBI categories. Furthermore, as we manage game caps, we are keeping **Yainer Diaz** (48.86) in the lineup despite a sub-50 score, as he is currently our best option at C1 given that **Cal Raleigh** is off today and **Will Smith** remains sidelined on the IL. We are tracking the health of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** closely as he continues his stint on the IL, hoping for a return to help stabilize our production in the coming weeks.",
